# Phase 6: threads, preemption, synchronisation, the 10-second
# producer/consumer run, latency, separate address spaces; then the thread
# list. The desktop must keep presenting frames while this runs.
sched: started
cerberus kernel shell
!send test sched
!wait 18
worker 1: count
worker 5: count
preemption: 5 busy threads interleaved
sleep: asked for 100 ms
mutex: 4 threads made 200000 increments, none lost
semaphore and reader-writer lock: correct
producer/consumer: 10 s
sums match, no deadlock
address spaces: two processes switched 4000 times, each always read its own value
wake-up latency: average
desktop: the compositor presented
cleanup:
test sched: PASS
!send ps
!wait 1
idle
reaper
shell
compositor
context switches
